lesson.example:
Assume a fictional site target.example allows users to claim 1 free 'Daily Gift' by clicking a button. The vulnerable backend code looks like this:

if (user.gifts_claimed < 1) {
  user.gifts_claimed++;
  awardGift(user.id);
}

An attacker uses a tool to send 20 requests to the '/claim-gift' endpoint at the exact same millisecond. Because the server is processing them all at once, the first step (checking if gifts_claimed is less than 1) returns 'True' for all 20 requests before the second step (adding 1 to the count) finishes for any of them. As a result, the user receives 20 gifts instead of 1. This is a classic Race Condition.
